From 11df503d119d118bc1631079592c86ed3caaaee3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:53:37 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(app,ui): name the setup carry's turn, stop counting
 dialog time as a freeze
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

#866: Setup2 held the part turned 90 degrees about X relative to Setup1,
a side-on turn the carried stock lattice refuses by design (lifting it
is #874, after the field engine #637). The relative-turn composition is
right; a test now pins that two setups turned alike carry.

- The carry refusal names the turn between the setups ("'Setup2' holds
  the part turned X -90°, Y 0°, Z 0° from how 'Setup1' holds it") and
  CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL reads in plain words; the setup page says what to
  do (choose "Its own stock", or hold the part as Setup1 does).
- "furniture" leaves the Settings page's active-setup radio and the
  Setups page footer.
- The 35 s "commands" slow frame was the user browsing in the modal
  file dialog: the dialog seam times every modal dialog and the frame
  watch takes that time off the frame it happened in.

Fixes #872
Fixes #873
Refs #866

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
